            "2. A stamen consists of a slender stalk called the <b>filament</b> and a terminal, swollen, two-lobed structure called the <b>anther</b>.",
            "3. Inside the microsporangia of the anther, microspore mother cells undergo meiotic division to produce thousands of microscopic, haploid <b>pollen grains</b>, which contain the male gametes.",
            "4. <i>Other structures:</i> Sepals are the outer protective green whorl (calyx), ovules are contained inside the ovary of the carpel/pistil, and the pistil is the entire female organ."
