            "2. <b>Absence of Fertilization:</b>",
            "The released unfertilized egg survives in the fallopian tube for approximately 24 hours. If sexual intercourse does not occur and the ovum is not fertilized by a sperm, fertilization fails.",
            "3. <b>Hormonal Withdrawal:</b>",
            "Without implantation, the temporary endocrine gland in the ovary (corpus luteum) degenerates, causing a sharp drop in blood levels of progesterone and estrogen.",
            "4. <b>Shedding of the Endometrium (Menstrual Bleeding):</b>",
            "Deprived of hormonal support, the thick, vascular uterine endometrial lining breaks down. The dead ovum, degenerated epithelial cells, mucus, and blood are shed and discharged from the body through the vagina. This process is called <b>menstruation</b>, typically lasting 3 to 5 days."
